# Files listed here are never sent to the Docker daemon (the "build context"),
# so `COPY . .` cannot put them in an image. Smaller context = faster build,
# and no local secret or host-specific artefact can leak into a layer.

# Installed and generated on the host (Windows binaries, dev caches): the
# image installs and builds its own, for Linux.
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist
coverage
src/generated
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*

# Secrets and local configuration: injected when the container starts
# (`--env-file`, Compose `environment`), never baked into the image.
.env
.env.*

# Not needed to build or run the app.
.git
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
docs
*.md
*.pdf

# Any other dot-file or dot-folder at the root (editor and tooling config).
.*
